cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "nsevt: Honest non-stationary extreme-value tail risk"
abstract: >-
  A small, dependency-light Python package for the honest analysis of trends in
  environmental extremes: bounded-tail detection via peaks-over-threshold GPD with
  profile-likelihood shape intervals and a bootstrap of the finite endpoint; a
  permutation-calibrated tail-scale trend test; Monte-Carlo power and
  minimum-detectable-effect analysis; multi-source transportability; block-conformal
  prediction bands valid under temporal dependence; and a two-scale Wasserstein
  distributional trend test.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Salomón Guzmán"
    given-names: "Elí Gaiska"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3533-3900"
    affiliation: "Colegio de Postgraduados, Campus Montecillo"
version: "0.1.0"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - extreme value theory
  - generalized Pareto distribution
  - non-stationarity
  - permutation test
  - conformal prediction
  - Wasserstein distance
  - climate extremes
repository-code: "https://github.com/GaiskaSalomon/nsevt"
